{{!-- The ▲▼ controls for a number input. The caller wraps its own `.stonetop-step` input and this
      partial in a `<span class="stonetop-stepper">`, so the input keeps its own attributes and stays
      a direct child (the CSS uses `:has(> …)`). One delegated handler drives every one of these —
      see src/utils/stepper.js. `upGlyph`/`downGlyph` replace the arrows where the buttons sit either
      side of the value rather than stacked beside it (the rail's bars). --}}
<button type="button" tabindex="-1" class="stonetop-stepper-btn stonetop-stepper-btn--up" data-step-dir="1">{{#if upGlyph}}{{upGlyph}}{{else}}▲{{/if}}</button>
<button type="button" tabindex="-1" class="stonetop-stepper-btn stonetop-stepper-btn--down" data-step-dir="-1">{{#if downGlyph}}{{downGlyph}}{{else}}▼{{/if}}</button>
